            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Domestic Policy and the \"Jamahiriya\" System</strong><br>\nGaddafi introduced the \"Jamahiriya,\" or \"state of the masses,\" in Libya, which he claimed was a form of direct democracy, though in practice it was considered authoritarian, with power concentrated in his hands.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Early Life and Education</strong></p>\n\n<p>Robert McNamara was born on June 9, 1916, in San Francisco, California. He studied at the University of California, Berkeley, and at Harvard Business School, where he learned to apply statistical analysis to business and war problems, a skill he would later use in government.<br>\nBusiness Career at Ford Motor Company</p>\n"
              },
